<meta type=article>
<title | ToC frame-skip — demo boxes never leak into the contents (#223/#246)>
<author | The Enscribe Team>
</meta>

<config toc=true toc-location=right toc-depth=3 />

<section #sec:real-a | First real section>

A real section. The two boxes below hold live-demo `<section>`s — a `<frame>`
(compiled to `<figure class="frameable-border">`) and an `<aside>`. Their inner
demo headings are box content, not page structure, so they must NOT appear in the
contents rail. This is the leak `collectEntries` fixed (#223/#246), mirroring the
client-side rail fix 4ece570.

<frame | A live-render demo box:
<section #sec:demo-frame | Frame demo heading>
This section is shown as demo content; it stays out of the contents.
>
>

An aside demo box:

<aside | An aside demo box:
<section #sec:demo-aside | Aside demo heading>
Likewise box content, never a contents entry.
>
>

<sub-section #sub:real | A real subsection>

A genuine nested subsection sitting OUTSIDE any box — ordinary section nesting, so
it still appears in the contents, nested under its parent section.

<section #sec:real-b | Second real section>

A second first-level section, outside any box — it still appears.
